From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PP: pack the per-hop tensors into one NCCL P2P

VLLM_PP_PACK_TENSORS_0029 (default 0; read once; the "pp" group exchanges
the value over its gloo group at start-up and every rank raises if the PP
ranks disagree). With the GLM mHC boundary plus the folded drafter fc
partial each hop carries two tensors ([rows,4,4096] bf16 hidden_states and
[rows,4096] fp32 aux_fc_partial), i.e. two NCCL SendRecv per hop per step.
When enabled, both sides derive the same byte layout from the (unchanged)
metadata: non-empty tensors sent whole (no TP all-gather slicing, or a
group of size 1) on the device type of the first such tensor, in dict order,
16-byte aligned, are copied into one uint8 buffer sent as the first device
P2P of the hop; the remaining tensors follow on the original path. The
receiver gets one buffer and returns dtype/shape views in the original key
order. Padded rows, dtypes and bytes on the wire are unchanged (at most 15
bytes of padding per segment); results are bit-identical. The pack copy runs
on the current stream before the isend is enqueued, so the source (the full
CUDA graph's persistent outputs) is no longer read by the send afterwards;
the buffer inherits the existing record_stream / pending-isend retention.
Composes with VLLM_PP_METADATA_CACHE_0025.

